# Settings Guide

## Overview

The Settings app is the central configuration interface for the Amiga. It provides comprehensive control over robot's configurations

## Features

### 1. About
- Display robot information (name, software version, installed apps)
- Access debug terminal for troubleshooting

### 2. WiFi
- Configure and manage network connections
- Select WiFi networks and enter credentials
- Enable/disable WiFi for testing
- Monitor connection status

### 3. Services
- View and control all Amiga services
- Toggle services on/off for troubleshooting
- Monitor service health and status

### 4. Robot Configuration

### 5. IMU Calibration
- Calibrate Inertial Measurement Unit
- Status indicator showing calibration state
- Essential for precise navigation
- Required after geometry changes

### 6. GPS NTRIP
- Configure RTK base station connection:
  - Server name/address
  - Mount point and port
  - Authentication credentials

### 7. PoE Switch Manager
- Network diagnostics and remote ping
- Per-port control for PoE devices
- Enable/disable individual ports
- Reset PoE switch functionality

### 8. Exit To Launcher

## Getting Started

### Accessing Settings

From the Launcher app on your device Tap the "Settings" icon to access the configuration interface

